{% set p = credentials_patroni %}
{% set b = credentials_pgbouncer %}
{% set h = credentials_haproxy %}
{% set nodes = groups['pg_nodes'] %}
{% set first = hostvars[nodes[0]].ansible_host %}
=====================================================================================
 {{ cluster_name }}  ({{ pgc_env }})  -  connection sheet
 Generated {{ now(utc=true).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC') }} by `make credentials ENV={{ pgc_env }}`
 CONTAINS PASSWORDS. Keep this file private (mode 0600); don't commit, mail or paste it.
=====================================================================================

ENDPOINTS
  Read/write (primary)   {{ cluster_vip }}:{{ h.haproxy_primary_port }}   VIP -> HAProxy -> pgbouncer -> current primary
  Read-only (replicas)   {{ cluster_vip }}:{{ h.haproxy_replica_port }}   VIP -> HAProxy -> pgbouncer -> a replica
  Allowed client nets    admin: {{ admin_cidrs | join(', ') or '-' }}   app: {{ app_cidrs | join(', ') or '-' }}
  Nodes:
{% for n in nodes %}
    {{ '%-22s' | format(n) }} {{ hostvars[n].ansible_host }}   (VM {{ hostvars[n].vm_id }} on {{ hostvars[n].vm_pve_node }})
{% endfor %}
  Find the current leader:
    ssh {{ vm_ci_user }}@{{ first }} sudo patronictl -c /etc/patroni/patroni.yml list

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POSTGRESQL SUPERUSER  (administration, dump restore)
  user      {{ p.patroni_superuser }}
  password  {{ vault_postgres_superuser_password }}
  Not allowed through the VIP or pgbouncer. Connect through an SSH tunnel to the LEADER's 127.0.0.1:5432:
    ssh -N -L 5433:127.0.0.1:5432 {{ vm_ci_user }}@<leader-ip>
    psql "host=127.0.0.1 port=5433 dbname=postgres user={{ p.patroni_superuser }}"
  pgAdmin: Connection  host 127.0.0.1, port 5432, user {{ p.patroni_superuser }}, SSL mode disable
           SSH Tunnel  host <leader-ip>, port 22, user {{ vm_ci_user }}, identity file = your SSH key
  After a failover the old leader is read-only: point the tunnel at the new leader.

APPLICATION / PERSONAL USERS
  Create them on the leader (runbook section 7), then connect through the VIP:
    psql "host={{ cluster_vip }} port={{ h.haproxy_primary_port }} dbname=<db> user=<user>"          # read/write
    psql "host={{ cluster_vip }} port={{ h.haproxy_replica_port }} dbname=<db> user=<user>"          # read-only
    postgresql://<user>:<password>@{{ cluster_vip }}:{{ h.haproxy_primary_port }}/<db>

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VM ACCESS
  SSH       ssh {{ vm_ci_user }}@<node-ip>        (key only; passwordless sudo)
  Console   user {{ vm_ci_user }}, password {{ vault_vm_ci_password }}   (Proxmox console only, not SSH)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERVICE ACCOUNTS  (used by the cluster itself; don't use them for applications)
  PostgreSQL replication   {{ p.patroni_replication_user }} / {{ vault_replication_password }}
  PostgreSQL pg_rewind     {{ p.patroni_rewind_user }} / {{ vault_rewind_password }}
  pgbouncer auth_query     {{ b.pgbouncer_auth_user }} / {{ vault_pgbouncer_auth_password }}
  Monitoring (exporters)   {{ credentials_postgres_exporter.postgres_exporter_user }} / {{ vault_monitoring_password }}
  Patroni REST (writes)    {{ p.patroni_restapi_user }} / {{ vault_patroni_restapi_password }}   http://<node-ip>:{{ h.haproxy_patroni_port }} (cluster nodes only)
  keepalived VRRP          VRID {{ pgc_environments[pgc_env].keepalived_vrid }}, auth_pass {{ vault_keepalived_auth_pass }}
  pgbouncer admin console  on a node: sudo -u postgres psql -h /run/pgbouncer -p {{ b.pgbouncer_port }} -U postgres pgbouncer
  etcd                     on a node: sudo /usr/local/bin/etcdctl-pgc endpoint health --cluster -w table
                           (TLS, certificates in /etc/etcd/tls; CA in inventories/{{ pgc_env }}/pki/)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROXMOX
  API         https://{{ pve_api_host }}:8006
  Token id    {{ vault_pve_api_token_id }}
  Token       {{ vault_pve_api_token_secret }}
  Template    VM {{ pve_template_vmid }} on {{ pve_template_node }}; storage {{ pve_storage }}; pool {{ pve_pool }}

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MONITORING  (reachable from {{ prometheus_server_ip }} only)
  node 9100, postgres 9187, pgbouncer 9127, patroni 8008, haproxy 8404 (/stats also from admin nets), etcd 2381
  Scrape config: docs/prometheus/{{ cluster_name }}.yml
=====================================================================================
